{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QExponentialTaylor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QExponentialTaylor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Normed","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qExpSeries_classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qExpSeries_classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-exponential-taylor.lean#L125-L142","doc":"At q = 1, the q-exponential Taylor series recovers the ordinary\nexponential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qExponentialTaylor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qExponentialTaylor","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-exponential-taylor.lean#L69-L123","doc":"**Taylor series of e_q (substrate regime `q > 1`):** for `q > 1` the\nq-exponential series `Σ xⁿ/[n]_q!` is summable for every `x ∈ ℝ`.\nThe Jackson factorials grow super-geometrically\n(`[n+1]_q / [n]_q = (q^{n+1}−1)/(q^n−1) → q > 1`), so the ratio test\ngives radius of convergence `∞`.\n\n**Regime correction (2026-06-26).** The previous encoding asserted\nsummability for *all* `q ≠ 1` via an `axiom qExponentialTaylor_axiom`.\nThat statement is **false**: for `0 < q < 1` one has `[k]_q → 1/(1−q)`,\nso `[n]_q!` grows only geometrically and the series has *finite* radius\n`1/(1−q)` — not summable for `|x| > 1/(1−q)`. Asserting the general\nstatement as an axiom was therefore unsound; the axiom is removed and\nthe proposition is restated in the substrate regime `q > 1`\n(`q₀ ≈ 1.11`), where the \"convergent for all `x`\" claim of the\nmanuscript genuinely holds. The convergence proof itself (ratio test\nvia the Jackson-integer divergence `[n]_q → ∞`) awaits the\n`q`-analysis API.  Proved below directly: the Jackson-integer\ndivergence `[n+1]_q = (q^{n+1}−1)/(q−1) → ∞` (from `q^n → ∞` for\n`q > 1`) drives the ratio test. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-exponential-taylor","label":"prop:q-exponential-taylor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-exponential-taylor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qExpSeries","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qExpSeries","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-exponential-taylor.lean#L64-L67","doc":"Formal Taylor series of the q-exponential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.jacksonFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.jacksonFactorial","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-exponential-taylor.lean#L58-L62","doc":"Jackson factorial [n]_q! = ∏_{k=1}^n [k]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.jacksonInt_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.jacksonInt_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-exponential-taylor.lean#L42-L56","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical guarded geometric bracket.**\n\n`jacksonInt` is kept rather than aliased: downstream proofs rewrite with the\nclosed form `(1−qⁿ)/(1−q)` syntactically, and swapping the body for\n`qIntGeoCl`'s `Finset.sum` breaks them. The two orientations differ only by\nnegating numerator and denominator, so the definitions agree — proved here\nrather than asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.jacksonInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.jacksonInt","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/q-exponential-taylor.lean#L35-L40","doc":"Jackson integer [n]_q = (1 - q^n) / (1 - q) over a characteristic-zero\nfield where q ≠ 1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}